e support, against about $423,000 for Clark. Markets give Clark roughly a five percent chance. No public general-election polls exist, so the forecast rests on fundamentals, ratings, and pricing. Alfonso's openness to raising the voting age drew headlines but has not visibly changed the race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0554, "margin": -10.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0396, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0389, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0525, "margin": -12.5}]}